{"id":"f17t1","name":"Player Event Batches","lang":"pyspark","entry":"solve","params":["spark","input_dir"],"limit_s":30,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>Our video players do not send each event on its own: they collect events and upload them in batches, sometimes long after, when the device is back online. The upload service writes the batches it receives as JSON lines into files ending with <code>.jsonl</code>, at any depth of <code>input_dir</code>. A batch looks like this:</p>\n<pre>{\"batch_id\": \"b-17\", \"device\": \"tv-3\", \"sent_at\": \"2026-03-04T21:00:00Z\",\n \"events\": [{\"ago\": 600, \"type\": \"play\", \"content\": \"show-1\"},\n            {\"ago\": 120, \"type\": \"pause\", \"content\": \"show-1\"}]}</pre>\n<p>(on one line in the files). <code>ago</code> is the number of seconds between the event and the upload, so an event happened at <code>sent_at</code> minus <code>ago</code> seconds. When an upload times out, the player sends the same batch again with the same <code>batch_id</code>; the service keeps both, but it is one batch.</p>\n<p>The content team wants to know how long each content is watched. A device watches a content from a <code>play</code> event of that content until the next event of the same device, whatever its type (<code>pause</code>, <code>stop</code>, or a <code>play</code> of another content or of the same one), because a device plays one thing at a time. A <code>play</code> that is the last event known for its device is still running and is not counted yet. Event types may be written in any case.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return, for each content watched at least once, the columns <code>content</code>, <code>viewers</code> (long, number of different devices that watched it) and <code>watch_minutes</code> (double, total watched time in minutes, rounded to 1 decimal), sorted by <code>watch_minutes</code> descending, then <code>content</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p class=\"exf\"><code>input_dir/2026/03/04/up-1.jsonl</code></p><pre class=\"exv\">{\"batch_id\": \"b1\", \"device\": \"tv-3\", \"sent_at\": \"2026-03-04T21:00:00Z\", \"events\": [{\"ago\": 600, \"type\": \"play\", \"content\": \"show-1\"}, {\"ago\": 120, \"type\": \"pause\", \"content\": \"show-1\"}]}\n{\"batch_id\": \"b2\", \"device\": \"tv-3\", \"sent_at\": \"2026-03-04T22:00:00Z\", \"events\": [{\"ago\": 1800, \"type\": \"PLAY\", \"content\": \"show-1\"}, {\"ago\": 900, \"type\": \"play\", \"content\": \"show-2\"}, {\"ago\": 300, \"type\": \"stop\", \"content\": \"show-2\"}]}\n{\"batch_id\": \"b2\", \"device\": \"tv-3\", \"sent_at\": \"2026-03-04T22:00:00Z\", \"events\": [{\"ago\": 1800, \"type\": \"PLAY\", \"content\": \"show-1\"}, {\"ago\": 900, \"type\": \"play\", \"content\": \"show-2\"}, {\"ago\": 300, \"type\": \"stop\", \"content\": \"show-2\"}]}\n</pre><p class=\"exf\"><code>input_dir/2026/03/04/up-2.jsonl</code></p><pre class=\"exv\">{\"batch_id\": \"b9\", \"device\": \"phone-1\", \"sent_at\": \"2026-03-04T23:00:00Z\", \"events\": [{\"ago\": 3600, \"type\": \"play\", \"content\": \"show-2\"}, {\"ago\": 60, \"type\": \"Pause\", \"content\": \"show-2\"}, {\"ago\": 30, \"type\": \"play\", \"content\": \"show-1\"}]}\n</pre><p class=\"exf\"><code>input_dir/2026/03/04/up-2.json.tmp</code></p><pre class=\"exv\">{\n</pre><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>content</th><th>viewers</th><th>watch_minutes</th></tr><tr><td>show-2</td><td>2</td><td>69.0</td></tr><tr><td>show-1</td><td>1</td><td>23.0</td></tr></table></div><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 30 seconds (pyspark)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 2 GB<br><b>[input]</b> string input_dir (the path of a folder)<br><b>[output]</b> DataFrame with exactly the columns <code>content</code>, <code>viewers</code>, <code>watch_minutes</code>, in this order; rows in the order given by the statement</div>","starter":"import os\nfrom pyspark.sql import SparkSession, DataFrame, functions as F\n\n\ndef solve(spark: SparkSession, input_dir: str) -> DataFrame:\n    # write your code here\n    return spark.read.json(input_dir)\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["consigne longue","JSON imbriqué","lots renvoyés","intervalles lecture/pause"],"minutes":25,"source":"Kata Lab","howto":"<h5>Où écrire</h5><ol><li>Écris dans l'éditeur à droite, fichier <code>solution.py</code>.</li><li>Complète la fonction <code>solve(spark, input_dir)</code>. Garde son nom et ses paramètres : ce sont les tests qui l'appellent, avec leurs propres données. N'écris pas d'appel à la fonction toi-même.</li><li><code>spark</code> est une SparkSession déjà prête : ne crée pas la tienne.</li><li><code>input_dir</code> est le <b>chemin d'un dossier</b> (une chaîne). Ses fichiers sont listés à gauche de l'éditeur sous <b>Files</b> : clique sur un fichier pour le lire (lecture seule), puis sur <code>solution.py</code> pour revenir à ton code. Lis les fichiers à partir de <code>input_dir</code>, jamais d'un chemin écrit à la main : chaque test donne un autre dossier.</li></ol><h5>Ce que tu dois renvoyer</h5><ol><li>Ta fonction doit <b>renvoyer</b> le résultat avec <code>return</code>. Un <code>print</code> ou un <code>show()</code> ne compte pas : il sort seulement dans l'onglet <b>Console Output</b>.</li><li>Le DataFrame renvoyé doit avoir <b>exactement 3 colonnes</b>, avec ces noms et dans cet ordre : <code>content</code>, <code>viewers</code>, <code>watch_minutes</code>. Une colonne en plus (une colonne de calcul oubliée), un nom différent ou un autre ordre et le test est faux, même si les valeurs sont justes. Finis par un <code>select(...)</code> de ces colonnes.</li><li><b>L'ordre des lignes compte</b> : trie exactement comme l'énoncé le demande (<code>orderBy</code> à la fin).</li><li>Valeurs : les nombres sont comparés à 0,000001 près : arrondis seulement là où l'énoncé le demande, et au nombre de décimales demandé.</li></ol><h5>Lancer et vérifier</h5><ol><li>Spark tourne dans ton Codespace : au premier RUN TESTS de la séance, attends qu'il soit prêt (1 à 2 minutes). Ensuite chaque lancement prend quelques secondes.</li><li>Clique <b>RUN TESTS</b> (ou <code>Ctrl + Entrée</code>) : tes 2 tests visibles tournent.</li><li>Quand c'est bon, tu vois en vert <b>« Tests passed: 2/2. »</b>. Sinon, ouvre le test marqué <b>Wrong answer</b> : compare « Expected return value » et « Your return value », et clique <b>VIEW DIFF</b> pour colorer les cases différentes. <b>Runtime error</b> veut dire que ton code a planté : le message est dans le test.</li><li>Clique <b>SUBMIT</b> : ta note sur 100 compte aussi 6 tests cachés. Soumets dès que quelques tests passent, puis améliore et resoumets : c'est la dernière soumission qui compte.</li></ol>","files":{"root":"input_dir","files":{"2026/03/04/up-1.jsonl":"{\"batch_id\": \"b1\", \"device\": \"tv-3\", \"sent_at\": \"2026-03-04T21:00:00Z\", \"events\": [{\"ago\": 600, \"type\": \"play\", \"content\": \"show-1\"}, {\"ago\": 120, \"type\": \"pause\", \"content\": \"show-1\"}]}\n{\"batch_id\": \"b2\", \"device\": \"tv-3\", \"sent_at\": \"2026-03-04T22:00:00Z\", \"events\": [{\"ago\": 1800, \"type\": \"PLAY\", \"content\": \"show-1\"}, {\"ago\": 900, \"type\": \"play\", \"content\": \"show-2\"}, {\"ago\": 300, \"type\": \"stop\", \"content\": \"show-2\"}]}\n{\"batch_id\": \"b2\", \"device\": \"tv-3\", \"sent_at\": \"2026-03-04T22:00:00Z\", \"events\": [{\"ago\": 1800, \"type\": \"PLAY\", \"content\": \"show-1\"}, {\"ago\": 900, \"type\": \"play\", \"content\": \"show-2\"}, {\"ago\": 300, \"type\": \"stop\", \"content\": \"show-2\"}]}\n","2026/03/04/up-2.jsonl":"{\"batch_id\": \"b9\", \"device\": \"phone-1\", \"sent_at\": \"2026-03-04T23:00:00Z\", \"events\": [{\"ago\": 3600, \"type\": \"play\", \"content\": \"show-2\"}, {\"ago\": 60, \"type\": \"Pause\", \"content\": \"show-2\"}, {\"ago\": 30, \"type\": \"play\", \"content\": \"show-1\"}]}\n","2026/03/04/up-2.json.tmp":"{\n"}},"visible":[{"input":{"input_dir":{"__dir__":{"2026/03/04/up-1.jsonl":"{\"batch_id\": \"b1\", \"device\": \"tv-3\", \"sent_at\": \"2026-03-04T21:00:00Z\", \"events\": [{\"ago\": 600, \"type\": \"play\", \"content\": \"show-1\"}, {\"ago\": 120, \"type\": \"pause\", \"content\": \"show-1\"}]}\n{\"batch_id\": \"b2\", \"device\": \"tv-3\", \"sent_at\": \"2026-03-04T22:00:00Z\", \"events\": [{\"ago\": 1800, \"type\": \"PLAY\", \"content\": \"show-1\"}, {\"ago\": 900, \"type\": \"play\", \"content\": \"show-2\"}, {\"ago\": 300, \"type\": \"stop\", \"content\": \"show-2\"}]}\n{\"batch_id\": \"b2\", \"device\": \"tv-3\", \"sent_at\": \"2026-03-04T22:00:00Z\", \"events\": [{\"ago\": 1800, \"type\": \"PLAY\", \"content\": \"show-1\"}, {\"ago\": 900, \"type\": \"play\", \"content\": \"show-2\"}, {\"ago\": 300, \"type\": \"stop\", \"content\": \"show-2\"}]}\n","2026/03/04/up-2.jsonl":"{\"batch_id\": \"b9\", \"device\": \"phone-1\", \"sent_at\": \"2026-03-04T23:00:00Z\", \"events\": [{\"ago\": 3600, \"type\": \"play\", \"content\": \"show-2\"}, {\"ago\": 60, \"type\": \"Pause\", \"content\": \"show-2\"}, {\"ago\": 30, \"type\": \"play\", \"content\": \"show-1\"}]}\n","2026/03/04/up-2.json.tmp":"{\n"}}},"expected":{"columns":["content","viewers","watch_minutes"],"rows":[["show-2",2,69.0],["show-1",1,23.0]]}},{"input":{"input_dir":{"__dir__":{"a.jsonl":"{\"batch_id\": \"z\", \"device\": \"d\", \"sent_at\": \"2026-01-01T10:00:00Z\", \"events\": [{\"ago\": 90, \"type\": \"play\", \"content\": \"c\"}, {\"ago\": 0, \"type\": \"play\", \"content\": \"c\"}]}\n"}}},"expected":{"columns":["content","viewers","watch_minutes"],"rows":[["c",1,1.5]]}}],"hidden_n":6,"hidden":"","solution":""}